WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:06.170
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Thursday, November 26.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.200
Zoom in! Europe's Hera probe just snapped the crater NASA punched into an asteroid.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.450
It's stadium-sized.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.680
And in surveys, truly noticing nature went with a more meaningful life.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.760
An unreleased OpenAI model claims faster matrix maths,

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.850
the sums inside every AI. It's a preprint.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.280
DeepMind says its AI agents now run some Gemini experiments.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.680
Self-improvement? Still far off.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:51.310
A historian says OpenAI's AI found who likely drew a 200-year-old sketchbook,

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:52.350
in 22 minutes.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.150
And Melbourne scientists mimicked brain-implant scarring in a dish,

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.460
to help future implants last longer.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.160
On to longevity. Alzheimer's mini-brains spent 40 days in space,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.410
and changed differently depending on their genes.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.790
In mice, normal brain ageing and dementia start out alike,

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:14.380
then split as DNA damage piles up.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.060
Closer to home,

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:21.340
warmer nights went with poorer memory in nearly 1,900 Australians over 40.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.650
And in 40 years of Shark Bay data,

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.200
dolphins that kept a steady social circle lived longer.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.470
On to wellbeing. In a small trial,

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:36.990
one dose of psilocybin eased 15 veterans' anxiety for a year.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.540
And a Perth clinic joins a global psilocybin trial for PTSD,

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.770
aiming to recruit from December.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.180
Now, the catch.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:51.620
A new test found top AI agents fail over a third of everyday chores.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.610
And New York banned AI chatbot toys for five years,

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.500
to study what they do to kids.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.940
On the frontier,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:08.410
US regulators cleared SpaceX to launch up to a million AI data-centre satellites.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:15.090
XPeng gave its IRON humanoid a new AI brain, and a release date: mid-2027.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.450
Oh, and Earth has a bonus mini-moon,

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.660
just a few metres wide. It leaves December 7.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.590
Craters, mini-brains and old friends: the closer you look,

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.770
the richer life gets. Zoom in!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.500
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney tomorrow night.
